 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? It' easy to fix. Use a lighter shade at the base of your cheeks, and a darker one higher up where the light is. That highlights the contour and makes it look natural. For dry, use light dusting of powder that matches you. For oily, go for gel, it gives a fresh, clean look. Now use a clean brush for the middle layer, it applies evenly and you don't end up with shadows anywhere. Use a few drops of gel as base coat and top coat it with water. It' keep fresh for weeks.",
